# Poster of a three-day jazz festival, on one A3 page without margins. The night-blue background is a gradient in a
# Page overlay with a negative Layer. The moon and its rings are boxes with Corner radius: 50% made faint with
# Opacity; they go partly off the page, so they are Overlay inside a Page overlay with Overflow: clip, which cuts
# them at its edges. The waves are a small SVG, also faint. The title is set at 168 points in IBM Plex Serif with a
# negative Letter spacing, the ribbon across the corner is an Overlay rotated −12 degrees, and the programme is a
# Grid of three columns, one per night, with each time and act on the same baseline (Vertical: baseline in a Stack).
# At the foot, an Overlay anchored to the bottom of the page with the venue and a QR code that leads to the tickets.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A3
		Margin: 0
	Title: Blue Hour · A jazz weekend by the water
	Subject: Poster of the Blue Hour jazz festival, Port Ellery, 14 to 16 August 2026
	Language: en
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Id: night
			Offset: 0
			Layer: -3
			Box:
				Background: linear(180, #0B1530, #18254F, #2B2560)
		Page overlay:
			Id: sky
			Offset: 0
			Layer: -2
			Box:
				Overflow: clip
			Overlay:
				Id: ring-outer
				Offset: -10 -280 auto auto
				Opacity: 20%
				Block:
					Style: ring-outer
			Overlay:
				Id: ring-inner
				Offset: 60 -210 auto auto
				Opacity: 35%
				Block:
					Style: ring-inner
			Overlay:
				Id: moon
				Offset: 120 -150 auto auto
				Opacity: 85%
				Block:
					Style: moon
		Page overlay:
			Id: water
			Offset: auto 0 160 0
			Layer: -1
			Opacity: 70%
			Image: documents/poster/waves.svg
				Box:
					Width: 100%
		Overlay:
			Id: ribbon
			Offset: 58 auto auto 40
